course: dictionary
lesson: 11596
title: A formal word for clothes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Apparel is a formal word for clothes. You will mostly meet it in shops, adverts and old stories, rather than in everyday talk. «The shop sells sports apparel for runners.»
explain: Use the words around it to find the meaning. Sports and runners are the clues, so apparel means clothes worn for sport. Check by swapping in a word you know: «The shop sells sports clothes for runners» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Old books use apparel for fine clothes worn on a special day. «The princess put on her fine apparel for the ball.» The clues are fine and ball, which tell you the clothes were grand.
fact: Apparel means clothing, especially clothes of a certain kind.
fact: Apparel is uncountable: you say some apparel, not two apparels.
fact: In old stories, «apparel» can mean fine clothes for a special occasion.
fact: In everyday talk, we usually say «clothes» instead of apparel.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad's washerwoman disguise is very different from his grand motoring apparel.
exercise: «The shop sells sports apparel for runners.» What does apparel mean here? | *Clothing, such as shorts and running tops | A kind of shop | Shoes and balls for sport | Running races
exercise: «The princess put on her fine apparel for the ball.» What does fine apparel mean? | Her muddy work clothes | *Her fine clothes for a special occasion | A pair of old boots | Her school uniform
exercise: In everyday talk, what word do we usually say instead of apparel? | Equipment | Furniture | *Clothes | Weather
test: What does «outdoor apparel» mean? | *Clothing worn outdoors | Tents and sleeping bags | Cars for the countryside | Food for picnics
test: Which sentence uses apparel correctly? | The apparels were blue. | *I bought some apparel for the school trip. | We have many apparels. | I bought three apparels.
exam: What does apparel mean in «The queen's gorgeous apparel shone in the sun»? | Shiny metal armour | *Splendid clothes | Dusty curtains | A golden crown
